Below is the full log of an {n_hands}-hand Kuhn Poker match, written from the learner's point of view. Kuhn Poker uses three cards (Jack < Queen < King). Each player antes 1 chip and receives one card. Player 1 checks or bets 1 chip. If Player 1 checks, Player 2 checks (showdown) or bets; facing a bet, a player calls or folds. The opponent's card is revealed only at showdown.

The opponent is exactly one of these bot types:
{definitions}

Based only on the log, estimate the probability of each type.
Output JSON only. Report each probability with two decimal places (e.g., 0.37), summing to 1:
{{"probs": {{{prob_keys}}}, "prediction": "<one of the type labels>", "evidence": "one sentence"}}

<match>
{match_log}
</match>
